Z||000002||thomas_l||05-31-2001||09:04 AM||||I can only share what I found with changing my 87 GT from a 5sp to a 4sp. On mine, the clutch assy was the same except the release bearing was different. Turns out the clutch pack for a 86 Cavalier had all the right stuff in it. Not knowing how the shifter & cables would be on yours, that could be another issue. Maybe another duke owner can add something. On mine I ended up doing a bunch of fabrication that wasn't necessary now that I know much more than I did then about how everything mounts. My experience was that the parts are all readily available, you just have to be patient and creative when getting it together.||||reg||5
